[{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"CurrentModule = DynamicStructs","category":"page"},{"location":"#DynamicStructs","page":"Home","title":"DynamicStructs","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Documentation for DynamicStructs.","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Modules = [DynamicStructs]","category":"page"},{"location":"#DynamicStructs.NoFields","page":"Home","title":"DynamicStructs.NoFields","text":"NoFields\n\nPass to Base.propertynames, propertyvalues, or propertypairs to exclude field names.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"#DynamicStructs.OnlyFields","page":"Home","title":"DynamicStructs.OnlyFields","text":"OnlyFields\n\nPass to Base.propertynames, propertyvalues, or propertypairs to include only field names.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"#Base.propertynames","page":"Home","title":"Base.propertynames","text":"Base.propertynames(x, ::Type{NoFields}, private=false)\n\nExcludes field names.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#Base.propertynames-2","page":"Home","title":"Base.propertynames","text":"Base.propertynames(x, ::Type{OnlyFields}, private=false)\n\nIncludes only field names.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#DynamicStructs.isdynamic-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","title":"DynamicStructs.isdynamic","text":"isdynamic(x)\n\nCheck if x is an instance of a dynamic type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#DynamicStructs.isdynamictype-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","title":"DynamicStructs.isdynamictype","text":"isdynamictype(T)\n\nCheck if T is a dynamic type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#DynamicStructs.propertypairs-Tuple{Any, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Home","title":"DynamicStructs.propertypairs","text":"propertypairs(x, args...)\n\nGet a tuple of the current property names and values. args is propagated to Base.propertynames.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#DynamicStructs.propertyvalues-Tuple{Any, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Home","title":"DynamicStructs.propertyvalues","text":"propertyvalues(x, args...)\n\nGet a tuple of the current property values. args is propagated to Base.propertynames.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#DynamicStructs.@dynamic-Tuple{Expr}","page":"Home","title":"DynamicStructs.@dynamic","text":"@dynamic [mutable] struct ... end\n\nDefine a dynamic struct:\n\nInstances of dynamic structs have dynamic properties that can be added/deleted at runtime. These properties are similar to Any-typed fields of structs in terms of performance.\nFields remain statically typed and accessing them compiles similarly to structs, so performance should not be significantly affected.\nThe macro adds a hidden field for storing dynamic properties with lazy initialization, meaning that the underlying storage is not allocated until the first dynamic property is added.\nThe default constructors of dynamic structs accept keyword arguments for dynamic properties, with a Base.show method that reflects this. These are only present if the block is free of any non-field expressions, such as custom constructors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"macro"}]
